{"parentUuid":"3b210ecc-90f3-4b7c-bcda-09e11d7c458e","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a943432bf960b6017","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_012aqHntXiGqyRAP8oyuZ6SD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01XswCijNPKHLrAMAc2WJv3k","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"neural beam search ML-guided combinatorial NP-hard placement"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":6,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7414,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"output_tokens":248,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7414},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":6,"output_tokens":248,"cache_read_input_tokens":13121,"cache_creation_input_tokens":7414,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":7414,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxnzfnrEmjkrv236dY5","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"dba1f8ac-bc56-43e7-ba69-eba3fb095972","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:10.133Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"dcb649f9-f71b-462a-bf16-8efd6cd88c02","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a943432bf960b6017","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fw4QjfSBkWCDPz17LaJq5v","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"beam search variants combinatorial optimization 2024 2025 diverse stochastic\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Bi-Criteria Diverse Plan Selection via Beam Search Approximation | Proceedings of the International Symposium on Combinatorial Search\",\"url\":\"https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/SOCS/article/view/31557\"},{\"title\":\"Beam Search Integration\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/beam-search-integration\"},{\"title\":\"Simulation-guided Beam Search for Neural Combinatorial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=tYAS1Rpys5\"},{\"title\":\"Diverse Beam Search for Improved Description of Complex Scenes | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/361527139_Diverse_Beam_Search_for_Improved_Description_of_Complex_Scenes\"},{\"title\":\"Simulation-guided Beam Search for Neural Combinatorial Optimization | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/361981787_Simulation-guided_Beam_Search_for_Neural_Combinatorial_Optimization\"},{\"title\":\"Beam Search Strategy\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/beam-search-strategy\"},{\"title\":\"Modern Beam Search Techniques\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/beam-search-techniques\"},{\"title\":\"Memory-Enhanced Neural Solvers for Efficient Adaptation in Combinatorial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2406.16424v1\"},{\"title\":\"Adaptive Beam Search Strategies\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/flexible-and-adaptive-beam-search-strategies\"},{\"title\":\"Parallel Beam Search for Combinatorial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/fullHtml/10.1145/3547276.3548633\"}]\n\nI've completed a web search on beam search variants, combinatorial optimization, and recent developments in 2024-2025. Here's a summary of key findings:\n\n## Recent Developments in Beam Search for Combinatorial Optimization\n\n### Diverse Beam Search Variants\n\nVariants have emerged that hybridize beam search with genetic algorithms, stochastic and self-evaluation-driven search, or employ bidirectional or diversity-promoting strategies. A notable hybridization is the genetic beam search in semantic packet aggregation (SemPA-GBeam), where each generation combines \"beam selection\" with GA-inspired mutation.\n\n### Stochastic Approaches\n\nRecent work combines round-wise Stochastic Beam Search with an update strategy derived from a provable policy improvement. Additionally, for applications demanding output diversity, incorporate determinantal beam search or stochasticization via CPSBS with kernel-based interaction penalties.\n\n### Adaptive and Modern Strategies\n\nModern beam search strategies have evolved from static, fixed-width breadth-first variants into a family of highly adaptable, diversity-aware, and theoretically grounded algorithms, with recent methods introducing adaptive pruning, vectorization, and stochastic sampling to improve efficiency.\n\n### Application to Neural Combinatorial Optimization\n\nPre-trained policies are often combined with search procedures ranging from stochastic sampling, beam search, or Monte Carlo Tree Search to more advanced strategies like online fine-tuning or searching a space of diverse pre-trained policies.\n\n### Parallel and Scalable Implementations\n\nRecent parallel beam search implementations achieve intra-node parallel efficiency around 60–90% on large problem instances, with combined large beam widths enabling discovery of new best feasible solutions for difficult benchmark instances.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"e13755e8-eef2-4849-bf94-891c232d9704","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:16.876Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dcb649f9-f71b-462a-bf16-8efd6cd88c02","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3b210ecc-90f3-4b7c-bcda-09e11d7c458e","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a943432bf960b6017","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01G5dYtNWRCHy8Lzp12HdESp","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"IDA* RBFS SMA* memory bounded heuristic search modern applications\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Lecture 3 - Advanced Search Algorithm - Artificial Intelligence\",\"url\":\"https://users.encs.concordia.ca/~bjaumard/AI2019Hanoi/Lecture3_AdvancedSearch_Algortihm.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Efficient memory-bounded search methods Mikhail Simin – Arjang Fahim\",\"url\":\"https://cse.sc.edu/~mgv/csce580f11/gradPres/580f11SiminFahimIDAStar.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Memory-Bounded Heuristic Search Techniques - Algorithms\",\"url\":\"https://www.scribd.com/document/947103971/4-2-Ida-star-Rbfs-Sma-star\"},{\"title\":\"Memory Bound Heuristic Search: IDA* and RBFS Explained • Economics.Town\",\"url\":\"https://economics.town/ai-ml/memory-bound-heuristic-search-ida-rbfs/\"},{\"title\":\"4 INFORMED SEARCH AND EXPLORATION\",\"url\":\"http://aima.cs.berkeley.edu/4th-ed/pdfs/newchap04.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Lecture 6: Search 5 Victor R. Lesser CMPSCI 683 Fall 2010 This lecture\",\"url\":\"http://mas.cs.umass.edu/classes/cs683/lectures-2010/Lec6_Search5-F2010-4up.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Solving Large Problems with Heuristic Search\",\"url\":\"https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/11209/26420/20775\"},{\"title\":\"Memory-bounded search ( Memory Bounded Heuristic Search ) in AI - GeeksforGeeks\",\"url\":\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/artificial-intelligence/memory-bounded-search-memory-bounded-heuristic-search-in-ai/\"},{\"title\":\"AL3391 IDA*, RBFS, SMA*, learn to search better- memory bounded heuristic search #aisubject #cs3491 - YouTube\",\"url\":\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=C3Zdz5ESNRk\"},{\"title\":\"Lecture 16 memory bounded search | PPTX\",\"url\":\"https://www.slideshare.net/slideshow/lecture-16-memory-bounded-search/71585172\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's an overview of memory-bounded heuristic search algorithms and their applications:\n\n## Memory-Bounded Heuristic Search Algorithms\n\nMemory-bounded heuristic search techniques include Iterative-Deepening A* (IDA*), Recursive Best-First Search (RBFS), and Simplified Memory-Bounded A* (SMA*), which aim to maintain completeness and optimality while addressing the exponential memory requirements of traditional A* search algorithms.\n\n### Individual Algorithms\n\n**IDA* (Iterative-Deepening A*)**\nIDA* uses the f-cost (g+h) as a cutoff threshold instead of depth, and its great advantage is its linear space complexity, which is essential for very large graphs. However, the drawback of IDA* is that it \"forgets\" everything between iterations, leading to node re-generation and potential time loss.\n\n**RBFS (Recursive Best-First Search)**\nRBFS tries to solve this by retaining some vital memory: the f-cost of the best alternative path. RBFS is a recursive algorithm that mimics the best-first approach of A*, exploring the most promising path using the f-cost to guide its choice. Like IDA*, RBFS is also optimal if its heuristic is admissible, and it uses only linear space.\n\n**SMA* (Simplified Memory-Bounded A*)**\nSMA* proceeds like A*, expanding the best leaf until memory is full, then drops the worst leaf node and backs up the value of the forgotten node to its parent.\n\n### Modern Applications\n\nIn Artificial Intelligence, search algorithms are essential for tasks ranging from route planning in navigation apps to solving complex puzzles like the Rubik's Cube. Additionally, memory-bounded search is ideal for real-time and embedded systems by efficiently finding solutions on devices with limited resources.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"70ca0a87-0e9f-413d-9d58-960d55d99ce8","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:17.664Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3b210ecc-90f3-4b7c-bcda-09e11d7c458e","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"dba1f8ac-bc56-43e7-ba69-eba3fb095972","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a943432bf960b6017","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01XswCijNPKHLrAMAc2WJv3k","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"neural beam search ML-guided combinatorial NP-hard placement\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Simulation-guided Beam Search for Neural Combinatorial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/pdf?id=tYAS1Rpys5\"},{\"title\":\"Learning Beam Search: Utilizing Machine Learning to Guide Beam Search for Solving Combinatorial Optimization Problems | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-95470-3_22\"},{\"title\":\"Simulation-guided Beam Search for Neural Combinatorial Optimization | OpenReview\",\"url\":\"https://openreview.net/forum?id=tYAS1Rpys5\"},{\"title\":\"Utilizing Machine Learning to Guide Beam Search for Solving ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.ac.tuwien.ac.at/files/pub/huber-21.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"[2207.06190] Simulation-guided Beam Search for Neural Combinatorial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2207.06190\"},{\"title\":\"Neural Sequence Generation with Constraints via Beam Search with Cuts: A Case Study on VRP | Proceedings of the International Symposium on Combinatorial Search\",\"url\":\"https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/SOCS/article/view/31549\"},{\"title\":\"Graph Learning for Combinatorial Optimization: A Survey of State-of-the-Art | Data Science and Engineering | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s41019-021-00155-3\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - yd-kwon/SGBS: codes for the paper \\\"Simulation-guided Beam Search for Neural Combinatorial Optimization\\\"\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/yd-kwon/sgbs\"},{\"title\":\"Learning Beam Search: Utilizing Machine Learning to Guide Beam Search for Solving Combinatorial Optimization Problems | Machine Learning, Optimization, and Data Science\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/10.1007/978-3-030-95470-3_22\"},{\"title\":\"(PDF) Learning Beam Search: Utilizing Machine Learning to Guide Beam Search for Solving Combinatorial Optimization Problems\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/358329838_Learning_Beam_Search_Utilizing_Machine_Learning_to_Guide_Beam_Search_for_Solving_Combinatorial_Optimization_Problems\"}]\n\nI found comprehensive search results on this topic. Here's what the research shows:\n\n## Overview\n\nBeam search is a well-known incomplete breadth-first-search variant frequently used to find heuristic solutions to hard combinatorial optimization problems. The research in this area focuses on enhancing beam search with machine learning guidance to solve NP-hard problems more effectively.\n\n## Key Approaches\n\n**Learning Beam Search (LBS):**\nA Learning Beam Search approach uses a machine learning model for guidance, with learning performed by utilizing principles of reinforcement learning where LBS generates training data on its own by performing nested BS calls on many representative randomly created problem instances. This has been tested on well-known NP-hard problems such as the Longest Common Subsequence problem and the Constrained Longest Common Subsequence problem.\n\n**Simulation-Guided Beam Search (SGBS):**\nSimulation-guided beam search examines candidate solutions within a fixed-width tree search that both a neural net-learned policy and a simulation (rollout) identify as promising. SGBS combines MCTS with beam search specifically for solving combinatorial optimization problems, and performs rollouts for nodes identified as promising by the neural network, which acts as a recourse mechanism to rectify incorrect decisions by the network.\n\n## Applications\n\nThese approaches have been applied to a 3D packing problem, problems on graphs including minimum vertex cover and maximum cut, and graph coloring.\n\nThese methods represent the state-of-the-art in combining neural networks with beam search for solving hard combinatorial optimization problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"543c02e5-0a6a-41a4-a38b-c3324fe1e0bb","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:21.742Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"dba1f8ac-bc56-43e7-ba69-eba3fb095972","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
