{"parentUuid":"18fe143f-b813-4af7-be73-13865dec465f","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a943432bf960b6017","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01DaxFL9KZQcSXXdxeMh1HvM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SbEpXHhKuiQKiCG4qsiqDv","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"beam search 2D rectangle packing strip packing python library implementation"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4631,"cache_read_input_tokens":20535,"output_tokens":222,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4631},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":222,"cache_read_input_tokens":20535,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4631,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4631,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxpQhgctVjyBjHbYuFG","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"6aee5fbf-9a6a-4d28-ba73-a2e773ae4985","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:26.213Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"18fe143f-b813-4af7-be73-13865dec465f","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a943432bf960b6017","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018fr5zFbtu8PJbYmz2qK9CL","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"large neighborhood search vs beam search ALNS placement layout\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - N-Wouda/ALNS: Adaptive large neighbourhood search (and more!) in Python. · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/N-Wouda/ALNS\"},{\"title\":\"Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search (ALNS)\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/adaptive-large-neighborhood-search-alns-algorithm\"},{\"title\":\"6: Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search (ALNS) Algorithm | Download Scientific Diagram\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/figure/Adaptive-Large-Neighborhood-Search-ALNS-Algorithm_fig21_335833775\"},{\"title\":\"Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search - an overview | ScienceDirect Topics\",\"url\":\"https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/computer-science/adaptive-large-neighborhood-search\"},{\"title\":\"Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search: The Algorithm That Learns While It Works | by Mithil | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@mithil27360/adaptive-large-neighborhood-search-the-algorithm-that-learns-while-it-works-c35e3c349ae1\"},{\"title\":\"Exploring the Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search (ALNS) Algorithm: Enhancing Optimization in Complex Systems\",\"url\":\"https://www.track2training.org/2024/04/exploring-adaptive-large-neighborhood.html\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - RobbertReijnen/DR-ALNS: [ICAPS 2024] DR-ALNS: Deep Reinforced Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/RobbertReijnen/DR-ALNS\"},{\"title\":\"Improving adaptive large neighborhood search: an evaluation of parallel approaches with deep learning integration | Evolutionary Intelligence | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/article/10.1007/s12065-025-01115-w\"},{\"title\":\"An Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search Heuristic for the Electric Vehicle Routing Problems with Time Windows and Recharging Strategies - Duan - 2023 - Journal of Advanced Transportation - Wiley Online Library\",\"url\":\"https://onlinelibrary.wiley.com/doi/10.1155/2023/1200526\"},{\"title\":\"Large Neighborhood Search - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/09_lns.html\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, I can provide information about these optimization concepts:\n\n## Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search (ALNS)\n\nALNS is a metaheuristic framework that uses iterative destroy–repair cycles to explore large, complex solution spaces. The defining feature of ALNS is its destroy–repair mechanism: portions of the incumbent solution are deliberately removed (destroyed), and the resultant partial solution is reconstructed (repaired) using a diverse portfolio of operators.\n\nThe adaptive selection mechanism records the performance of each operator and dynamically adjusts the probability of selecting each based on historical effectiveness, thereby enhancing search efficiency and solution quality.\n\n## Large Neighborhood Search (LNS)\n\nLarge Neighborhood Search (LNS) offers a more efficient approach by formulating a \"mini-problem\" that modifies parts of the current solution, which often involves randomly selecting some variables, resetting them, and using constraint solvers to find the optimal new values within the context of the remaining solution.\n\n## Comparison and Applications\n\nThe search results don't provide a direct detailed comparison between beam search and LNS/ALNS for placement layout problems. However, when you have several neighborhood strategies, they can be dynamically integrated using an Adaptive Large Neighborhood Search (ALNS).\n\nALNS has been successfully applied to vehicle routing, scheduling, and packing problems by reliably delivering near-optimal solutions under tight constraints.\n\nIf you need more specific information comparing beam search to ALNS for placement layout problems, I could search for more targeted results on that comparison.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"5d73457b-25b2-45fe-ab75-6aab4ae05e41","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:32.020Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"18fe143f-b813-4af7-be73-13865dec465f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"34286d25-6998-425a-beea-53a6a02e40fd","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a943432bf960b6017","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01MptrAsN3BKJKpZLLXN15XC","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"beam search warm start CP-SAT MIP solver hint heuristic incumbent\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Heuristics as warm start for Mixed Integer Programming (MIP) models | Towards Data Science\",\"url\":\"https://towardsdatascience.com/heuristics-as-warm-start-for-mixed-integer-programming-mip-models-9046781dd21f/\"},{\"title\":\"How does it work? - The CP-SAT Primer - Using and Understanding Google OR-Tools' CP-SAT Solver\",\"url\":\"https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/07_under_the_hood.html\"},{\"title\":\"User MIP start did not produce a new incumbent solution/ Another try with MIP start – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/360073235912-User-MIP-start-did-not-produce-a-new-incumbent-solution-Another-try-with-MIP-start\"},{\"title\":\"Warm Start Optimization. Some introduction to the concept of… | by AlainChabrier | Medium\",\"url\":\"https://medium.com/@AlainChabrier/warm-start-optimization-ac73eef189e9\"},{\"title\":\"Starting from a solution: MIP starts\",\"url\":\"https://www.ibm.com/docs/en/icos/22.1.0?topic=mip-starting-from-solution-starts\"},{\"title\":\"A Heuristic Algorithm Based on Beam Search and Iterated Local Search for the Maritime Inventory Routing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/html/2505.13522\"},{\"title\":\"Update parameters if MIP start does not produce a solution – Gurobi Help Center\",\"url\":\"https://support.gurobi.com/hc/en-us/community/posts/33622798256785-Update-parameters-if-MIP-start-does-not-produce-a-solution\"},{\"title\":\"Beam search - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beam_search\"},{\"title\":\"Exploiting the Power of mip Solvers in maxsat | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-642-39071-5_13\"},{\"title\":\"[2505.13522] A Heuristic Algorithm Based on Beam Search and Iterated Local Search for the Maritime Inventory Routing Problem\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.13522\"}]\n\nI've completed the web search for your query about beam search warm start CP-SAT MIP solver hint heuristic incumbent. Here are the key findings:\n\n## Key Concepts Found\n\n**Beam Search:** Beam search is a heuristic search algorithm that explores a graph by expanding the most promising node in a limited set, and it is a modification of best-first search that reduces its memory requirements.\n\n**Warm Start and Incumbent Solutions:** An incumbent is the best feasible solution found at each step of the algorithm. Providing a MIP start helps improve time to optimal solution by using the value of a feasible initial solution to prune some parts of the search tree, and heuristics may also be used by the engine to improve this initial solution.\n\n**CP-SAT Solver:** The search results reference the CP-SAT solver from Google OR-Tools. Once a feasible solution is discovered, incomplete subsolvers take over, applying local search heuristics such as Large Neighborhood Search (LNS), and these subsolvers attempt to improve the solution by iterating through various strategies.\n\n**Hints vs. Incumbent:** One approach when a MIP Start does not produce an incumbent solution is to use the MIP start values as variable hints.\n\n**Practical Application:** In some research, a warm-up phase was performed to obtain an initial good solution, which was then used to warm-start the solver, with subsequent experiments carried out for extended periods.\n\nThe search results indicate that combining heuristics like beam search with warm-start techniques can significantly improve MIP solver performance by providing better initial solutions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"54f1c3dd-7248-4c3f-abb1-940b5964313d","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:32.841Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"34286d25-6998-425a-beea-53a6a02e40fd","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"6aee5fbf-9a6a-4d28-ba73-a2e773ae4985","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a943432bf960b6017","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01SbEpXHhKuiQKiCG4qsiqDv","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"beam search 2D rectangle packing strip packing python library implementation\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"GitHub - secnot/rectpack: Python 2D rectangle packing library · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/secnot/rectpack\"},{\"title\":\"rectpack · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/rectpack/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - seanys/2D-Irregular-Packing-Algorithm: Realize 2D irregular packing algorithm with python · GitHub\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/seanys/2D-Irregular-Packing-Algorithm\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - javier-martinez-palmer/rectpack: Python 2D rectangle packing library\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/javier-martinez-palmer/rectpack\"},{\"title\":\"rectangle-packer\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/rectangle-packer/\"},{\"title\":\"Extra material: Strip packing — Hands-On Mathematical Optimization with AMPL in Python\",\"url\":\"https://ampl.com/mo-book/notebooks/03/strip-packing.html\"},{\"title\":\"rectangle-packing-solver · PyPI\",\"url\":\"https://pypi.org/project/rectangle-packing-solver/\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - findux/rectpack: Python 2D rectangle packing library\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/findux/rectpack\"},{\"title\":\"A Beam Search Approach Based on Action Space for the 2D Rectangular Packing Problem | SpringerLink\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-981-13-1651-7_14\"},{\"title\":\"GitHub - Sammbale7/rectpack: Python 2D rectangle packing library\",\"url\":\"https://github.com/Sammbale7/rectpack\"}]\n\nBased on the web search results, here are the key findings related to your query:\n\n## Python Libraries for 2D Rectangle Packing\n\n**Rectpack** is a prominent Python library for 2D rectangle packing. Rectpack is a collection of heuristic algorithms for solving the 2D knapsack problem, also known as the bin packing problem, essentially packing a set of rectangles into the smallest number of bins.\n\nThis library implements three of the algorithms described in literature: Skyline, Maxrects, and Guillotine, with the following variants.\n\n**Other Python Libraries:**\n- A solver to find a solution of the 2D rectangle packing problem by simulated annealing (SA) optimization is available through the `rectangle-packing-solver` package.\n\n## Beam Search for 2D Rectangle Packing\n\nA beam search algorithm is presented to solve the 2D rectangular packing problem, with basic algorithms working according to 7 rule vectors of heuristic selection rules designed to select a corner-sticking action. This was published in academic literature (Yin et al., 2018).\n\n## Strip Packing\n\nFor strip packing specifically, strip packing refers to the problem of packing rectangles onto a two dimensional strip of fixed width, with the most basic variant being to pack a set of rectangles onto the shortest possible strip without rotation.\n\nThe search results show that while beam search approaches have been studied academically for rectangle packing, the popular open-source Python libraries like Rectpack primarily use heuristic algorithms (Skyline, Maxrects, Guillotine) rather than explicit beam search implementations.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"30a33dd8-68ea-4bd1-ad73-f8ddfee47018","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:35.570Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6aee5fbf-9a6a-4d28-ba73-a2e773ae4985","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
