{"parentUuid":"9b8070a4-b3ef-40a1-98c0-09a373139b35","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a943432bf960b6017","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_014DcZ4SHjgvBpBjVUTtYSzC","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01DtECDhx5outqgNWPPcbRLx","name":"WebSearch","input":{"query":"beam search competitive ratio approximation guarantee NP-hard theoretical"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4381,"cache_read_input_tokens":25166,"output_tokens":153,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4381},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":153,"cache_read_input_tokens":25166,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4381,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4381,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxqQvMdXnumrQNDGNzv","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"b4df7652-abb8-4448-92fa-0d4bdd4552e6","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:42.471Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"9b8070a4-b3ef-40a1-98c0-09a373139b35","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a943432bf960b6017","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01McppUBUizZP59L7WGMa3xY","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"bidirectional A* search 2024 graph search engineering library\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Bidirectional Search - GeeksforGeeks\",\"url\":\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/dsa/bidirectional-search/\"},{\"title\":\"VNS-BA*: An Improved Bidirectional A* Path Planning Algorithm Based on Variable Neighborhood Search - PMC\",\"url\":\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC11548247/\"},{\"title\":\"Bidirectional Search : Two-End BFS\",\"url\":\"https://www.thealgorists.com/Algo/TwoEndBFS\"},{\"title\":\"Bidirectional Search in Graph - Naukri Code 360\",\"url\":\"https://www.naukri.com/code360/library/bidirectional-search-in-graph\"},{\"title\":\"Bidirectional Search in AI - GeeksforGeeks\",\"url\":\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/bidirectional-search-in-ai/\"},{\"title\":\"Bidirectional search - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bidirectional_search\"},{\"title\":\"Two new bidirectional search algorithms - Illinois Experts\",\"url\":\"https://experts.illinois.edu/en/publications/two-new-bidirectional-search-algorithms/\"},{\"title\":\"Bidirectional Search for Path Finding | Baeldung on Computer Science\",\"url\":\"https://www.baeldung.com/cs/bidirectional-search\"},{\"title\":\"Focused Bidirectional Search Trees: A Bidirectional Optimal Fast Matching Method for Robot Path Planning | Request PDF\",\"url\":\"https://www.researchgate.net/publication/374080775_Focused_Bidirectional_Search_Trees_A_Bidirectional_Optimal_Fast_Matching_Method_for_Robot_Path_Planning\"},{\"title\":\"Single-Frontier Bidirectional Search Ariel Felner\",\"url\":\"https://cdn.aaai.org/ojs/7555/7555-13-11085-1-2-20201228.pdf\"}]\n\nI've performed a web search for \"bidirectional A* search 2024 graph search engineering library\". Here are the key findings:\n\n## Overview of Bidirectional A* Search\n\nBidirectional search is a graph search algorithm which finds the smallest path from source to goal vertex. It runs two simultaneous searches - Forward search from source/initial vertex toward goal vertex and Backward search from goal/target vertex toward source vertex, replacing a single search graph (which is likely to grow exponentially) with two smaller sub graphs – one starting from initial vertex and other starting from goal vertex.\n\n## Recent Research and Developments (2024)\n\nThe A* algorithm is a global path planning method based on graph search, which improves upon blind search algorithms by utilizing heuristic information from the map to selectively expand path nodes, providing advantages such as high search efficiency and simplicity.\n\nBidirectional rectangular expansion has been developed, effectively reducing the number of expansions and accelerating the algorithm.\n\n## Algorithm Variants\n\nRecent research has focused on various improvements:\n- Two new bidirectional heuristic search algorithms for solving the shortest path problem on graphs are consistent-heuristic bucket-based bidirectional search (CBBS) and front-to-front GPU bidirectional search (FFGBS).\n- A new type of bidirectional search called Single-Frontier Bidirectional Search (SFBDS) has been introduced.\n\nThe search results primarily focus on algorithmic research rather than specific engineering libraries, though applications include robotics path planning, navigation systems, and optimization problems.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"d9716e40-09b6-464d-8ef5-0c31549e5c16","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:47.426Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"9b8070a4-b3ef-40a1-98c0-09a373139b35","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"b4df7652-abb8-4448-92fa-0d4bdd4552e6","isSidechain":true,"promptId":"5ea2c3ce-bea8-4ce3-8195-f1f0f2991204","agentId":"a943432bf960b6017","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DtECDhx5outqgNWPPcbRLx","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"beam search competitive ratio approximation guarantee NP-hard theoretical\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Approximate Muscle Guided Beam Search for Three-Index Assignment Problem\",\"url\":\"https://arxiv.org/pdf/1703.01893\"},{\"title\":\"Learning Beam Search: Utilizing Machine Learning to Guide Beam Search for Solving Combinatorial Optimization Problems | Springer Nature Link\",\"url\":\"https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-3-030-95470-3_22\"},{\"title\":\"Beam search - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beam_search\"},{\"title\":\"Parallel Beam Search for Combinatorial Optimization\",\"url\":\"https://dl.acm.org/doi/fullHtml/10.1145/3547276.3548633\"},{\"title\":\"Approximation algorithms for NP-hard problems\",\"url\":\"https://hochbaum.ieor.berkeley.edu/html/pub/Book:Approximation-Algorithms-for-NP-Hard-Problems.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"Modern Beam Search Techniques\",\"url\":\"https://www.emergentmind.com/topics/beam-search-techniques\"},{\"title\":\"Approximation Algorithms - GeeksforGeeks\",\"url\":\"https://www.geeksforgeeks.org/dsa/approximation-algorithms/\"},{\"title\":\"Approximation algorithm - Wikipedia\",\"url\":\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Approximation_algorithm\"},{\"title\":\"Improved Beam Search Diversity for Neural Machine ...\",\"url\":\"https://web.stanford.edu/class/archive/cs/cs224n/cs224n.1194/reports/custom/15709706.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"How to Implement a Beam Search Decoder for Natural Language Processing - MachineLearningMastery.com\",\"url\":\"https://machinelearningmastery.com/beam-search-decoder-natural-language-processing/\"}]\n\nBased on the search results, here's what I found regarding beam search and its relationship to competitive ratio, approximation guarantees, and NP-hard problems:\n\n## Key Findings\n\n**Beam Search and NP-Hard Problems:**\nThe Three-Index Assignment Problem (AP3) is a well-known NP-hard problem, and beam search is used as part of heuristics to develop algorithms that achieve a good trade-off between solution quality and running time. Similarly, beam search has been applied to NP-hard optimization problems including Permutation Flow Shop Scheduling and the Traveling Tournament Problem.\n\n**Approximation Guarantees:**\nSince a goal state could potentially be pruned, beam search sacrifices completeness and is not optimal (there is no guarantee that it will find the best solution). However, recent research advances have generalized beam search in terms of adaptivity, diversity, efficiency, optimality guarantees, and application domain, while introducing analytical frameworks to capture trade-offs and theoretical properties.\n\n**Theoretical Developments:**\nMore recent work shows progress on theoretical aspects. For navigable graphs, adaptive beam search using a distance-based stopping rule provides a formal bound on the quality of returned neighbors relative to the true minimum distance. Additionally, path-max enforced beam search ensures non-increasing solution costs as beam width increases.\n\nThe search results indicate that while beam search itself does not provide direct competitive ratio guarantees, modern research is increasingly providing theoretical analysis and formal guarantees under specific conditions.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"uuid":"3ada4e64-eea2-4e99-acd0-351b3565cca3","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:02:50.331Z","sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b4df7652-abb8-4448-92fa-0d4bdd4552e6","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
{"parentUuid":"3ada4e64-eea2-4e99-acd0-351b3565cca3","isSidechain":true,"agentId":"a943432bf960b6017","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Q3HZB3nV1poPfYRGBjAQsv","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I have enough material. Let me compile the report.\n\n---\n\n# Heuristic Search 变体调研：能否作 ALNS 之外的 warm-start 备选\n\n## 1. 主要 search variant 横向对比\n\n| 算法家族 | 现代状态 | 内存特性 | 与组合优化契合度 | 可用工具 |\n|---------|---------|---------|----------------|---------|\n| **Classical Beam Search** | 活跃。成熟的 NP-hard heuristic 主力 | 线性 O(B·d) | 高，已用于 3D packing / 2D rectangle / scheduling / VRP | 自己写约 200-500 行；NeuroLogic、SGBS（GitHub yd-kwon/SGBS） |\n| **Diverse Beam Search (DBS)** | NLP 起源，2024 已推广到 SOCS（symbolic combinatorial search）做 plan diversity | 同 BS | 中-高，避免 beam 收敛同一区域 | fairseq beam（NLP 向）；Vijayakumar 原始实现 |\n| **Stochastic Beam Search** | 2024-2025 仍在迭代，结合 policy improvement / determinantal kernel | 同 BS | 中，能跳脱局部最优 | 需自己写，无主流通用库 |\n| **Simulation-Guided Beam Search (SGBS)** | KAIST 2022 论文，活跃 baseline，把 MCTS rollout 嵌进 beam | 中（B·rollouts） | 高，专为 NCO 设计 | yd-kwon/SGBS GitHub repo |\n| **Learning Beam Search (LBS)** | 用 RL 训练 evaluation function 替换 hand-crafted heuristic | 同 BS | 高，但要训练数据 | TU Wien Huber 2021 实现，需自己改 |\n| **IDA*** | 教科书算法，工业用主要在 puzzle / pathfinding | O(d) 极省 | **低**。对最大空矩形+设施摆放这种 wide branching、状态空间不规则的问题，threshold 反复迭代代价巨大 | networkx 没有；自己写很容易但意义不大 |\n| **RBFS** | 同上，更省时间但仍需要 admissible h | O(d) | 低，理由同 IDA* | 学术参考 |\n| **SMA*** | 90年代经典，工业实际应用很少 | 用满给定 memory | 低-中 | 几乎无现成库 |\n| **Bidirectional A*** | 2024 SOCS 仍出新算法（CBBS、FFGBS、SFBDS） | O(节点) | **不适用**。需要明确 source/goal，placement 没有\"反向终点\" | NetworkX、OMPL（机器人） |\n\n## 2. 跟我们 placement 的契合度\n\n- **状态空间形状**：266 个 mandatory 设施 × 70×70 网格 + ghost rectangle，每步决策\"放下一个设施在哪\"=> wide branching factor，state 比较容易 evaluate（已放置的+ghost area）。这正是 beam search 的甜点区，IDA* 的死穴。\n- **没有自然 goal state**：266 个全放完才算\"完整解\"，但中间状态质量可比较 => beam 的 partial-solution 评估很自然。\n- **min_side ≥ 6 的可行性约束**：beam 节点扩展时硬剪枝，活节点数会被压得很小。\n- **Bidirectional / IDA* 不适用**：没有目标终点 + 状态空间没有自然 cost-threshold 结构 => IDA*/RBFS/SMA*/Bidirectional 全部排除，**这次调研可以直接跳过这一支**。\n\n## 3. 跟 LNS / ALNS / RINS 关系\n\n- **Beam search = 构造性 heuristic**（从空解构造一条 partial → full solution 的路径），LNS/ALNS = 改进式 heuristic（destroy-repair 一个完整解）。两者**正交互补**，不是替代。\n- 标准管线：beam search 产 incumbent → 喂给 LNS/ALNS 改进 → 喂给 CP-SAT 当 hint。Maritime Inventory Routing 论文（arXiv:2505.13522）就是 BS+ILS 这套组合。\n- **RINS** 需要 LP relaxation，CP-SAT 没暴露这个接口 => 不直接可用。\n- **CP-SAT 的 LNS 是内置的**（subsolver），所以\"先 beam 后 LNS\"不需要我们再写 LNS。\n\n## 4. 给 CP-SAT 当 hint 的可行性\n\nCP-SAT 接受 `model.add_hint(var, value)` —— 把 beam 产的整解（每个 facility 的位置 + ghost rect 顶点）作为 var hint。CP-SAT 会用 `fix_variables_to_their_hinted_value` LNS subsolver 验证 hint 可行性，可行就纳入 incumbent，不可行就丢弃。这是低风险接入：beam 失败不会污染 exact 路径，符合 AI Safety Contract 的 hint-only 原则。\n\n## 5. 工程量评估\n\n| 项目 | 估时 | 风险 |\n|-----|-----|-----|\n| Vanilla beam search（B=64-256，evaluation = area + min_side + 启发式 lookahead） | 3-5 天 | 低，纯构造算法 |\n| 加 stochastic 扰动 + diverse beam（避免 wave 间撞同一布局） | +1-2 天 | 低 |\n| 接入 hint pipeline，跟 ALNS 共存（two-stage warm-start） | +1 天 | 低 |\n| SGBS / 神经引导 | +2-3 周（要训练数据） | 高，违反\"shadow-only sidecar\"要走 D 通道 |\n\n**初版只做 vanilla + diverse 即可，神经版是 Phase 3C 才考虑的事。**\n\n## 6. 是否值得作 ALNS 之外的 warm-start 备选\n\n**值得，但定位是\"ALNS 的前置构造器\"，不是平行替代。**\n\n理由：\n1. **填补能力空白**：ALNS 需要初始解，目前我们靠 CP-SAT 自己启动慢热阶段。Beam search 在几秒内能产可行解（266 设施 × 70×70 在 B=128 量级完全跑得动），直接缩短 ALNS 启动时间。\n2. **工程量小**：vanilla beam 一周内可上线，远低于神经引导/IDA* 重写代价。\n3. **与 exactness constitution 兼容**：纯 hint，不写 checkpoint，不参与 proof，符合 AI Safety Contract 的 order_only / hints-only 边界。\n4. **可作 Lane B (deterministic tuning) 子项目**：不需要训练数据，可复现，符合 deterministic 要求。\n\n**不建议作的部分**：IDA* / RBFS / SMA* / Bidirectional 全部不适用我们的问题结构，这次调研可以直接 close 掉这条线，不再投入。\n\n**建议落地路径**：在 `src/search/` 下新增 `beam_warm_start.py`，B=128 + diverse beam，输出 `data/checkpoints/beam_hints/*.json`（注意：这是 hint 文件，不是 checkpoint，命名要避开），由 outer_search 在 wave 启动时通过 `model.add_hint` 注入 CP-SAT，跟现有 ALNS 串联（beam → ALNS refine → CP-SAT prove）。\n\nSources:\n- [Simulation-guided Beam Search for Neural Combinatorial Optimization](https://arxiv.org/abs/2207.06190)\n- [SGBS GitHub repo (yd-kwon/SGBS)](https://github.com/yd-kwon/sgbs)\n- [Learning Beam Search (Huber, TU Wien)](https://www.ac.tuwien.ac.at/files/pub/huber-21.pdf)\n- [Beam Search + ILS for Maritime Inventory Routing (arXiv 2505.13522)](https://arxiv.org/abs/2505.13522)\n- [Parallel Beam Search for Combinatorial Optimization (ACM)](https://dl.acm.org/doi/fullHtml/10.1145/3547276.3548633)\n- [Bi-Criteria Diverse Plan Selection via Beam Search (SOCS)](https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/SOCS/article/view/31557)\n- [Neural Sequence Generation with Beam Search Cuts: VRP (SOCS)](https://ojs.aaai.org/index.php/SOCS/article/view/31549)\n- [CP-SAT Primer: LNS & solution hints](https://d-krupke.github.io/cpsat-primer/09_lns.html)\n- [ALNS Python package (N-Wouda/ALNS)](https://github.com/N-Wouda/ALNS)\n- [DR-ALNS: Deep Reinforced ALNS (ICAPS 2024)](https://github.com/RobbertReijnen/DR-ALNS)\n- [A Beam Search Approach for 2D Rectangular Packing](https://link.springer.com/chapter/10.1007/978-981-13-1651-7_14)\n- [rectpack Python library](https://github.com/secnot/rectpack)\n- [Solving Large Problems with Heuristic Search (JAIR)](https://www.jair.org/index.php/jair/article/download/11209/26420/20775)"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2740,"cache_read_input_tokens":29547,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2740,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"}},"requestId":"req_011CaoxrVnabacfZHU8kKppk","attributionAgent":"general-purpose","type":"assistant","uuid":"8153c08c-3443-47b4-85ef-b23f550bd926","timestamp":"2026-05-07T22:03:51.472Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"D:\\claude pj\\zmd\\.upstream_clones","sessionId":"7db7f276-a2bf-4762-b9b8-bb35f8cf3fb9","version":"2.1.128","gitBranch":"master","slug":"squishy-zooming-sphinx"}
